<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oman</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oman is a country on the south-eastern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a>, commanding the approaches to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>. In antiquity it was known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magan">Magan</a>, a source of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in the age of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>. In the eighteenth century parts of it, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a>, were briefly held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oman.jpg" alt="Oman" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sakralamn · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nakhal_Fort_Sultanate_of_Oman_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
